IMPORT prelude

-- Misrepresentation Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- (plain-text rendering of the Singapore Statutes Online text; not the official text).
-- LAYER 1, SECTION 3.  Written from the text alone; nobody's point of view.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  Every rule answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the
-- text itself gives; NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts and is never to be read as no.
-- Every fact is a MAYBE BOOLEAN input: NOTHING stands for a fact that was not given.  Each branch that
-- answers no carries "FALSE-kind" and the words of the text that say it; each branch that answers NOTHING
-- carries "NOTHING-kind" and why.  (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".)
--
-- "In so far as": the text lets a term be of no effect only in part.  Each rule below is asked of the term, or
-- of the part of it, that is in question; the text does not say how a term is divided into parts.
-- The requirement of reasonableness is section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977, which is not among
-- the sources: whether a term satisfies it is a fact the caller states (a court's judgment, never guessed).

§ `Section 3 -- Avoidance of provision excluding liability for misrepresentation`

-- src:83 | 3. If a contract contains a term which would exclude or restrict —
-- src:85 | (a) any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject
-- src:86 | by reason of any misrepresentation made by him before the
-- src:87 | contract was made; or
-- src:90 | (b) any remedy available to another party to the contract by
-- src:91 | reason of such a misrepresentation,
@ref s 3(a) and (b) (src:83-91)
GIVEN `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "(a) ... or (b) ...": either limb is enough
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a contract contains a term which would exclude or restrict — (a) any liability ... (b) any remedy ..." (an "if" condition fails: neither limb)
        IF `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the answer turns on was not given (an input is NOTHING), and the text decides nothing without it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:93 | that term shall be of no effect except in so far as it satisfies the
-- src:94 | requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair
-- src:95 | Contract Terms Act 1977, and it is for those claiming that the term
-- src:96 | satisfies that requirement to show that it does.
@ref s 3 (src:93-96)
GIVEN `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 the term is of no effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a contract contains a term which would exclude or restrict —" (an "if" condition fails: this section does not reach the term)
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as it satisfies the requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977" (the exception is met, so the term is not of no effect)
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the text's yes: "that term shall be of no effect"
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the answer turns on was not given (an input is NOTHING), and the text decides nothing without it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 3 "it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does" (src:95-96)
GIVEN `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the party asked about is one of those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a contract contains a term which would exclude or restrict —" (an "if" condition fails: the section, and so the burden it places, does not arise)
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the text's yes: "it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does"
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the party asked about is one of those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the burden is placed on "those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement" and the text says nothing of a party who makes no such claim
        IF `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the party asked about is one of those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the answer turns on was not given (an input is NOTHING), and the text decides nothing without it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The burden read with the bar.  "That term shall be of no effect except in so far as it satisfies the requirement ... and it is for
-- those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does."  The function above takes the requirement as a
-- fact the caller states.  This one takes it as what those claiming it have SHOWN: where they have not shown that the term satisfies
-- the requirement, the requirement is not met for the purpose of this answer, so a term within (a) or (b) is of no effect.  The
-- text puts the showing on them and says nothing of the standard of proof; "shown" is a fact the caller states (NOTES.md, F10).
-- src:93 | that term shall be of no effect except in so far as it satisfies the
-- src:94 | requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair
-- src:95 | Contract Terms Act 1977, and it is for those claiming that the term
-- src:96 | satisfies that requirement to show that it does.
@ref s 3 "it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does" (src:93-96)
GIVEN `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement have shown that it does` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` MEANS
    -- The showing stands in for the requirement: shown is the exception met (JUST FALSE for no effect); not shown is the exception
    -- not met (JUST TRUE for no effect, for a term within (a) or (b)); not given is NOTHING.  Whether the section reaches the term
    -- is decided by the function above, which answers JUST FALSE for a term outside (a) and (b).
    `s 3 the term is of no effect` `the term would exclude or restrict any liability to which a party to a contract may be subject by reason of a misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made` `the term would exclude or restrict any remedy available to another party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation` `those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement have shown that it does`
